## Third-party components

DragonSlayer dynamically links or bundles the following third-party components,
each under its own licence:

- **libgphoto2** — LGPL-2.1+ (http://gphoto.org)
- **libusb** — LGPL-2.1+ (https://libusb.info)
- **ffmpeg** — LGPL / GPL depending on build (https://ffmpeg.org). DragonSlayer
  invokes ffmpeg as an external process; it is not statically linked.
- **Zadig / libwdi** — LGPL-3.0 (https://zadig.akeo.ie, https://github.com/pbatard/libwdi).
  Bundled unmodified in the Windows release; used only for the one-time WinUSB
  driver installation on the user's own machine.
- **egui, eframe, wgpu** — MIT / Apache-2.0 dual (https://github.com/emilk/egui)
- **image** — MIT / Apache-2.0 dual (https://github.com/image-rs/image)
- **serde, tokio, clap, thiserror** and other Rust crates — MIT / Apache-2.0
  as declared in their respective `Cargo.toml` files. Full list produced by
  `cargo tree` on a release build.

## No warranty, no support

The MIT terms above are the operative legal statement.
In plain English:

- Use it however you like.
- Fork it, sell it (there's nothing to sell), modify it, ship it inside
  something else — you don't need to ask.
- Keep the copyright and licence notice.
- If it eats your homework, that's on you.

There is no support, no guaranteed response to bug reports, no roadmap and no
SLA. The maintainers work on this in their own time and may stop at any
moment. If you need something reliable and supported, buy commercial software.
